-f04e9e113bb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074380/assets/404c1f68f360e2916a6281033c8a7e9771b648c61156da903ce2f66b931b924e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380895} :answer-field/id #uuid "55884eef-95e5-5e34-af7c-f78ee79a7cdd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380890}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c24f9a28-e384-580a-a49f-58c03f2a6551" :question/math-academy-id "q-333274" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=6x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=6y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could represent the phase portrait of the decoupled system above?" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSince our system is decoupled, its eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\lambda }_{2}=6$ with the corresponding eigenvectors $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nThe general solution of the system is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{6t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{6t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]={e}^{6t}[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nNotice that for each vector $[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ we get the straight-line solutions of the form\n${e}^{6t}[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$\nthat represent the line passing through the origin and parallel to the vector $[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSince ${e}^{6t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions move away from the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nAmong the given options, the only phase portrait satisfying these conditions is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074380/assets/404c1f68f360e2916a6281033c8a7e9771b648c61156da903ce2f66b931b924e.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380896 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2c335ee-467a-5114-a7d9-4c2692562d9e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Phase Portrait of a System With Repeated Eigenvalues"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9e9c641-5b84-5bd1-a69d-1df5d2af2e93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t{e}^{-4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380898} {:answer/id #uuid "4ca46fad-b8f8-5b07-9ba2-8f61592ba62a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380899} {:answer/id #uuid "b463a777-5b7a-5859-86c6-db709fe6d3a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t{e}^{4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380900} {:answer/id #uuid "9cac7af0-cd1e-5dc7-824e-d62a64ef03bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380901}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ca46fad-b8f8-5b07-9ba2-8f61592ba62a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380899} :answer-field/id #uuid "86aa0fe3-9b2c-5357-b81e-0cf721fd39bd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380897} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3a97f29-3eab-50ae-a276-0f0faa1ddd66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380903} {:answer/id #uuid "c83adfd9-b01d-5ba4-b9cf-0bd5b4fb6e3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380904} {:answer/id #uuid "0e79b901-9c78-55c9-b9d3-ef13ee13ace0" :answer/ty